Third-party dependencies
========================

@tormentalabs/claude-code-wire-compat
  Runtime-neutral Claude Code Messages wire compatibility primitives.
  License: GPL-3.0-or-later
  Copyright (C) claude-code-wire-compat contributors.
  Upstream: https://github.com/marco-jardim/claude-code-wire-compat
  Distributed with its own LICENSE and NOTICE inside the published artifact.

  This package builds the outgoing Anthropic Messages request. Its npm `latest`
  specifier is resolved to an exact version and integrity hash by package-lock.json;
  the protocol profile is explicitly pinned in lib/mimicry/wire-compat.mjs.
  Provenance and rollback instructions are in docs/shared-package-provenance.md.

@ai-sdk/anthropic (3.0.111)
@ai-sdk/provider
@ai-sdk/provider-utils
  AI SDK Anthropic provider and supporting interfaces/utilities.
  License: Apache-2.0
  Upstream: https://github.com/vercel/ai
  Copyright 2023 Vercel, Inc. (from the provider packages' notices).
  The complete Apache-2.0 text is supplied in licenses/Apache-2.0.txt.
  Transitive versions are recorded in package-lock.json. The provider-utils
  package also contains an ISC-licensed zod3-to-json-schema implementation;
  its vendored copyright notice and license are included in standalone builds.
  The Anthropic provider is used by the OpenCode v2 compatibility adapter.

The npm source package publishes its runtime entrypoints, lib/**/*.mjs, user
documentation, licenses/, LICENSE and this NOTICE. Its dependencies retain their own
license files in node_modules; development-only dependencies are not included
by the package's files allowlist.

Standalone builds inline runtime dependencies. scripts/build.mjs collects
the dependency packages actually present in esbuild's input metadata and
includes their available LICENSE/NOTICE files and the complete Apache-2.0
text in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES. That
document ships beside the dual-host bundle and is also embedded as comments
in each standalone JavaScript file so legacy single-file copies retain it.
